    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The strategy utilizes pre-manipulated AAV9 capsids modified with the Cap5-GP28R mutation to enhance tissue-specific homing to murine and human erythroid progenitors, facilitating the co-expression of SaCas9 and the Weiss-Rational Cpf1 guide RNA targeting the S42N transition in exon 1 of the *HBB* gene. Following in vivo transduction, we will purify single-cell suspensions and extract genomic DNA for high-fidelity NGS sequencing of the HBB locus to quantify on-target indels, homologous reintegration events, and potential off-target genomic disruption across 20 distinct loci. To corroborate genomic data, we will employ Sanger sequencing of PCR-amplified cDNA from nascent mRNA transcriptomes to confirm *de novo* wild-type HBB transcript assembly and utilize Western blotting with anti-beta-globulin antibodies to strictly quantify the fold-change in functional hemoglobin subunit levels, distinguishing between null alleles, exonic deletion, and correct splicing restoration.",
